THE DELIVERABLE: A REPLACEMENT FOR SHUFFLE_MAX = 0.60
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
cross_subject.py:146 holds its label-shuffle leakage guard to a hard-coded
0.60. That is a round number with no derivation anywhere in the repo. Below it is
replaced by a measured quantile of the CORRECT reference distribution.

  BLOCK null (correction (b)), on the k/900 lattice:
    99.0th percentile = 53.1% (478/900)   <- proposed replacement for SHUFFLE_MAX
    99.5th percentile = 53.4% (481/900)   <- the more conservative option
  GLOBAL null (what the repo currently permutes), for comparison:
    99.0th percentile = 54.2% (488/900)
    99.5th percentile = 54.7% (492/900)

  Where the existing 0.60 sits:
    in the BLOCK null : +7.81 sd, percentile 100.00, 0 of 2000 draws at or above it
    in the GLOBAL null: +5.19 sd, percentile 100.00, 0 of 2000 draws at or above it
    against the OBSERVED cross-subject result 59.4% (535/900): the guard sits +0.6 points from it

  Replacement lands ABOVE 0.60: False
  What this does NOT show: none of these quantiles was validated against a REAL
  leak. cross_subject.py:143 already discloses that its guard has never fired.
  Replacing an underived threshold with a derived one does not measure the guard's
  false-alarm rate against an actual defect.

